   "xml_index": 1,
   "xml_name": "PS8_001_DEBUG Sorted Copy",
   "display_name": "Sorted Copy",
   "questiontext_html": "<p><b>This is a DEBUG-TYPE question. Please read this carefully, it works differently from the other questions.</b></p>\n<p>The answer box below already contains a complete function. For the one example test shown below, this function gives the correct output.</p>\n<p><b>But the function has a mistake</b> (possibly more than one). For some other valid inputs, which we have <b>not</b> shown you, it gives a wrong answer or stops with an error.</p>\n<p><b>What you need to do:</b></p>\n<ol><li>Read the code carefully and trace it in your head for different valid inputs, to find the inputs where it goes wrong.</li><li>Fix the mistake(s), so that the function works correctly for <b>all</b> valid inputs described below.</li><li>Add a short comment in the code saying which line(s) you changed and why.</li></ol>\n<p><b>How this question is checked:</b> this question has some <b>hidden tests</b> that check exactly those inputs. When you click <b>Check</b>, we run your code on the example test and on the hidden tests. The pre-filled code will fail at least one hidden test; once you have fixed the mistake(s) correctly, all tests will pass.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><b>The function:</b> <code>sorted_copy(L)</code> takes a list of integers <code>L</code> and <b>returns</b> a <b>new</b> list with the same items sorted from smallest to largest. It must <b>not change</b> <code>L</code> itself: after the call, <code>L</code> must still be in its original order.</p>\n<p><b>Your fixed function must work for:</b> any list of integers, including an empty list.</p>\n<p><b>Example test (already passes):</b> <code>sorted_copy([3, 1, 2])</code> returns <code>[1, 2, 3]</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "# The code below has a bug. It will not work correctly for some\n# valid inputs other than the one shown in the example.\n# Identify the BUG and CORRECT it. Add a comment saying what you changed.\n\ndef sorted_copy(L):\n    L.sort()\n    return L\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "print(sorted_copy([3, 1, 2]))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "[1, 2, 3]",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": true,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "L = [3, 1, 2]\nS = sorted_copy(L)\nprint(S)\nprint(L)",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "[1, 2, 3]\n[3, 1, 2]",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "L = [9, -1, 4, 4]\nsorted_copy(L)\nprint(L)",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "[9, -1, 4, 4]",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(sorted_copy([]))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "[]",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    }
   ]
  },
